Z||000007||william_thorniii||02-05-2001||12:03 PM||||RaeQwan,<P>I feel your pain man.  I recently lost a pet.  My mother always said that he was my "son" since the wife and I do not want any children.  <P>My dog was poisoned with rat poison.  He died on January 11.  He suffered several strokes just trying to get him to the vet.  I will not forget the pain that he went through.. it was truly an awful way to die.  <P>The worst part of the whole thing was that he was an inside dog.  He would only be outside for a few minutes a day (he hated being out).  Someone actually came into the yard and fed him through the fence.  Footprints were observed in the 6" of snow on the far side of the house at his time of death.  <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||13
Z||000008||87ECO5||02-05-2001||01:19 PM||||I felt badly when you first told me this, William, and I still feel the same way.<P>Sometimes I wish I had the ability to provide answers to things like this.  I wish I could tell you who harmed your dog.<P>I like to think of myself as a kind and gentle person.  But, when I hear about things like this, I want to find the son of a b*tch and cram rat poison down his f#@king throat!||||reg||8
